<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Land Apportionment Act</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1930">1930</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Land Apportionment Act of 1930 was a law of the British colony of Southern Rhodesia that divided land by race. It reserved about half of the country, including the best farmland and the towns, for the small white minority and confined Africans, the great majority, to native reserves and purchase areas. It remained the basis of land policy until 1969 and fuelled the grievances behind the liberation war.</p></div>
